Z||000008||wkayl||04-19-2001||08:12 PM||||Do your laundry and think about it.  I had some very collectable Coca-Cola signs (four 10 ft metal bottle from the late 60's new in the crate).  I sold 3 of them in the 80's to put a new top on my Buick conv.  I was kicking myself for years after until my dad's barn fell down and smashed everything left in there.  I still have the one in my garage. <P>By the way, is the price any where close to what we paid for my daughter's 88 Formula? Probably not, <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/twocars.jpg"> ||||reg||14
Z||000009||Old Lar||04-19-2001||08:12 PM||||As with any collectable, it is what you want it for.  I have my Fieros to drive, if you want a Fiero for a car on a pedestle, keep it.  If you want it for an investment, forget it not many cars appreciate like a stock portfolio.<P>Soon I'll have my hands on that steering wheel, I got from you via Tim.  If you hadn't sold it to me, it would be still be sitting on a shelf in its box. No value to you, but it looks good in my car.||||reg||3
Z||000010||RRobinson||04-19-2001||08:44 PM||||Mike,<P>I could sense your hesitation in our recent correspondence. My advice: keep it until you are SURE you want to part with it. I for one would rather have the Formula than the 2000 Trans Am (although I love the F-body). <P>Ryan<BR>88 GT<BR>2-87 GTs<BR>87 SE V6<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000011||mrfiero||04-19-2001||09:05 PM||||Wkayl,<P>Multiply your Formulas cost by 11 and you'd be close to the price of the silver one.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><BR>Larry,<P>I really wish I still had that steering wheel......it wold go great with my brand new tan 5sp. console and leather shift knob! <P>For those who don't know....way back in 1994 I bought the very last '88 tan leather GT steering wheel available from GM.  A few years later I sold/traded it to Tim at Fiero Parts who then sold it to Larry (who in turn installed it on his GT).  I have regretted selling it ever since and have now acquired several other NOS '88 tan stuff that would complement that steering wheel very nicely.  Oh well.<P>Ryan,<P>It's always hard for me to part with any of my cars....even the higher mileage ones (like Wkayl's Formula).  I wish I were loaded.....then I'd buy up and hoard every Fiero!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>I'll let you know what I figure out within the timeframe that we discussed. <P>If anything......I know where there are a few more low mileage Formulas (114 mi., 231 mi. & 1331 mi.)......two have T-Tops.  Maybe (if I decide to keep mine) you'd be interested in one of these?   All are burgundy (medium red metallic) with gray interiors and 5-sp. trannies.<BR>   <P>  ||||reg||1
