Z||000019||mrfiero||04-23-2001||01:18 AM||||Kelvin,<P>That's how I feel.  There are plenty of higher mileage Fieros out there that there is no need to drive the lower mileage ones.  Although, after owning a 300 mile Fiero, I no longer consider 16K miles "low".  I still drive my GT every once in a while, although I do it illegally.  To keep myself from drivng it every day I never registered it.  I figured if it doesn't have plates I won't be tempted.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><BR>Ross,<P>It was a tough call, but I was/am going broke keeping them.  I love my GT too much, so the Formula had to go.  I would also love to have the TA, but not right now......maybe after I get a "real" job. <P>Barc still has a few Fieros and they are for sale......I think one of those burgundy T-Top Formulas would look great in your garage!  To refresh your memory.....both are fully loaded (as many options that a Formula can get) 5-speeds.  One has 114 miles the other has 232.  LMK if you're interested and I'll relay that to Barc.||||reg||1
